{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\ndef build_prime_list(max_val):\n    prime_list = []\n    for num in range(2, max_val):\n        prime_check = True\n        for p in prime_list:\n            if p * p > num:\n                break\n            if num % p == 0:\n                prime_check = False\n                break\n        if prime_check:\n            prime_list.append(num)\n    return prime_list\n\nprimes = build_prime_list(6000)\n\ndef get_prime_factors(n):\n    factor_counts = {}\n    for p in primes:\n        if p * p > n:\n            break\n        if n % p == 0:\n            count = 0\n            while n % p == 0:\n                n //= p\n                count += 1\n            factor_counts[p] = count\n    if n > 1:\n        factor_counts[n] = 1\n    return factor_counts\n\ndef list_divisors(n):\n    factors = get_prime_factors(n)\n    divisors = [1]\n    for prime, exp in factors.items():\n        extended = []\n        for d in divisors:\n            power = 1\n            for _ in range(exp + 1):\n                extended.append(d * power)\n                power *= prime\n        divisors = extended\n    return divisors\n\ndef compute_value(n, mod):\n    memo = {0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 2}\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        value = 2 * memo[i - 1]\n        for divisor in list_divisors(i):\n            if 2 <= divisor <= i:\n                value += memo[i // divisor] - memo[(i - 1) // divisor]\n                value %= mod\n        memo[i] = value % mod\n    return memo[n]\n\nn_input, m_input = map(int, input().split())\nprint(compute_value(n_input, m_input))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static List<Integer> primes = buildPrimeList(6000);\n\n    private static List<Integer> buildPrimeList(int maxVal) {\n        List<Integer> primeList = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int num = 2; num < maxVal; num++) {\n            boolean primeCheck = true;\n            for (int p : primeList) {\n                if (p * p > num) {\n                    break;\n                }\n                if (num % p == 0) {\n                    primeCheck = false;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n            if (primeCheck) {\n                primeList.add(num);\n            }\n        }\n        return primeList;\n    }\n\n    private static Map<Integer, Integer> getPrimeFactors(int n) {\n        Map<Integer, Integer> factorCounts = new HashMap<>();\n        for (int p : primes) {\n            if (p * p > n) {\n                break;\n            }\n            if (n % p == 0) {\n                int count = 0;\n                while (n % p == 0) {\n                    n /= p;\n                    count++;\n                }\n                factorCounts.put(p, count);\n            }\n        }\n        if (n > 1) {\n            factorCounts.put(n, 1);\n        }\n        return factorCounts;\n    }\n\n    private static List<Integer> listDivisors(int n) {\n        Map<Integer, Integer> factors = getPrimeFactors(n);\n        List<Integer> divisors = new ArrayList<>();\n        divisors.add(1);\n        \n        for (Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> entry : factors.entrySet()) {\n            int prime = entry.getKey();\n            int exp = entry.getValue();\n            List<Integer> extended = new ArrayList<>();\n            \n            for (int d : divisors) {\n                int power = 1;\n                for (int i = 0; i <= exp; i++) {\n                    extended.add(d * power);\n                    power *= prime;\n                }\n            }\n            divisors = extended;\n        }\n        return divisors;\n    }\n\n    private static int computeValue(int n, int mod) {\n        Map<Integer, Integer> memo = new HashMap<>();\n        memo.put(0, 0);\n        memo.put(1, 1);\n        memo.put(2, 2);\n        \n        for (int i = 3; i <= n; i++) {\n            int value = (2 * memo.get(i - 1)) % mod;\n            \n            for (int divisor : listDivisors(i)) {\n                if (divisor >= 2 && divisor <= i) {\n                    int term = (memo.get(i / divisor) - memo.get((i - 1) / divisor)) % mod;\n                    value = (value + term) % mod;\n                }\n            }\n            memo.put(i, (value % mod + mod) % mod);\n        }\n        return memo.get(n);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n_input = scanner.nextInt();\n        int m_input = scanner.nextInt();\n        System.out.println(computeValue(n_input, m_input));\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.202533692587167e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.7788631743751466e-05, -1.597391747054644e-05, -0.0013344916515052319, -0.023770008236169815, -7.510157047363464e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -3.0278701160568744e-05, -0.2519296109676361, -0.02630358189344406, -0.05299525707960129, -2.503391897334